{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>הואיל</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: כי הואיל ה' לעשות, הואיל הלך אחרי צו — this is what was said: in either case they are called children of the Place — those who do the will of the Place by fulfilling the Torah, which is הואיל משה, and those who serve idolatry, which is הלך אחרי צו — הואיל ה' לעשות אתכם לו לעם." "<b>את התורה הזאת לאמר</b> and adjacent to it: יהוה אלהינו — i.e., He warned them about the unity of the Name."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The three Masorah citations are unaddressed in the original; identified as Deuteronomy 1:5 (here), 2:30, and 2:30 respectively, based on the phrase הואיל ה' לעשות and הלך אחרי צו."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:27.864987714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}